          <br />
            In life, everyone has to make several important decisions about their lives like who to get married, what kind of profession he should occupy or if it is preferred, which university to study. All of these vital decisions are made by that person on their behalf. Similarly, decision-making over the fate of other living creatures is in the hand of human-being as well. Nevertheless, humans are on the verge of losing our capability to choose out of different options as a consequence of technological disruption. The development of advanced IT technologies makes us desperate to solve our problems. 
            I am going to dive much deeper into the drama of decision-making, we are getting used to let algorithms to make decisions for us. Due to that fact that they collect enormous amount of our biometric data from our smart bracelets and intelligent webcam, the ability of algorithms to predict our wishes is increasing significantly. By the midst of this century, the probability of making mistakes in decision making will reach roughly zero. By then, AI tells us who to marry, what to do tomorrow, what kind of food we consume. When you are searching for relevant and trustworthy information, we increasingly rely on Google for answers, so our ability to search information independently diminishes. Already today, “Truth” is defined by the top results of the Google search.
        </p>
